FUN_002482-T1	4956.XP_002496354.1	4.06e-309	848.0	28PDH@1|root,2QW0Y@2759|Eukaryota,39V1W@33154|Opisthokonta,3P0BY@4751|Fungi,3QQJN@4890|Ascomycota,3RT86@4891|Saccharomycetes,3RYGD@4893|Saccharomycetaceae	4751|Fungi	K	Component of the Mediator complex, a coactivator involved in the regulated transcription of nearly all RNA polymerase II-dependent genes. Mediator functions as a bridge to convey information from gene-specific regulatory proteins to the basal RNA polymerase II transcription machinery. Mediator is recruited to promoters by direct interactions with regulatory proteins and serves as a scaffold for the assembly of a functional preinitiation complex with RNA polymerase II and the general transcription factors	MED1	GO:0000122,GO:0000428,GO:0005575,GO:0005622,GO:0005623,GO:0005634,GO:0005654,GO:0005667,GO:0006355,GO:0006357,GO:0008150,GO:0009889,GO:0009890,GO:0009891,GO:0009892,GO:0009893,GO:0010468,GO:0010556,GO:0010557,GO:0010558,GO:0010604,GO:0010605,GO:0010628,GO:0010629,GO:0016591,GO:0019219,GO:0019222,GO:0030880,GO:0031323,GO:0031324,GO:0031325,GO:0031326,GO:0031327,GO:0031328,GO:0031974,GO:0031981,GO:0032991,GO:0043226,GO:0043227,GO:0043229,GO:0043231,GO:0043233,GO:0044422,GO:0044424,GO:0044428,GO:0044446,GO:0044451,GO:0044464,GO:0044798,GO:0045892,GO:0045893,GO:0045934,GO:0045935,GO:0045944,GO:0048518,GO:0048519,GO:0048522,GO:0048523,GO:0050789,GO:0050794,GO:0051171,GO:0051172,GO:0051173,GO:0051252,GO:0051253,GO:0051254,GO:0055029,GO:0060255,GO:0061695,GO:0065007,GO:0070013,GO:0070847,GO:0080090,GO:0090575,GO:1902494,GO:1902679,GO:1902680,GO:1903506,GO:1903507,GO:1903508,GO:1990234,GO:2000112,GO:2000113,GO:2001141	-	ko:K15145	-	-	-	-	ko00000,ko03021	-	-	-	Med1
